.TH URAN 1 "August 2026" "GNU/Uran 1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
uran \- generate random numbers using /dev/urandom

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B uran
[\fI\,OPTIONS\/\fR]

.SH DESCRIPTION
.B uran
generates random numbers using the system entropy source
.IR /dev/urandom .
It supports range limiting, multiple values, and various output formats.
.PP
By default, it prints a single 32-bit unsigned integer.

.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-count = \fI\,N\/\fR
Generate N random numbers. Default: 1.
.TP
.BR \-m ", " \-\-min = \fI\,N\/\fR
Set minimum value of the range. Default: 0.
.TP
.BR \-M ", " \-\-max = \fI\,N\/\fR
Set maximum value of the range.
Default: maximum 32-bit value (4294967295).
.TP
.BR \-x ", " \-\-hex
Output numbers in hexadecimal format.
.TP
.BR \-o ", " \-\-octal
Output numbers in octal format.
.TP
.BR \-b ", " \-\-binary
Output numbers in binary format.
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-separator = \fI\,STRING\/\fR
Use STRING as a separator between numbers.
Default: newline character.
.TP
.BR \-N ", " \-\-nonblock
Use non-blocking entropy source. If insufficient entropy is available,
falls back to blocking mode automatically.
.TP
.BR \-\-version
Show version information and exit.
.TP
.BR \-\-help
Show this help message and exit.

.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Successful completion.
.TP
.B 1
Error (invalid arguments, read failure, etc.).

.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Generate one random number (default):
.B uran
.TP
Generate 5 numbers in range 1-10:
.B "uran -n 5 -m 1 -M 10"
.TP
Generate 3 hexadecimal numbers separated by commas:
.B "uran -n 3 -x -s \",\""
.TP
Generate a 12-character ASCII password (codes 33-126):
.B "uran -n 12 -m 33 -M 126 -s \"\""
.TP
Generate without blocking on low entropy:
.B "uran -N -n 3"

.SH BUGS
Range validation prevents overflow by using 64-bit arithmetic internally.
Uniform distribution is guaranteed through rejection sampling.

